  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The findings are based on a literature review rather than primary empirical data or simulations of specific port operations.",
      "what": "This study analyzes the conditions under which ports can accelerate the adoption of low-emission trucks for hinterland transport. Using a multi-system transition framework, it maps the technological, actor, and institutional connections between hinterland transport and port energy systems under EU and port authority regulations, identifying nine distinct conditions that facilitate this transition.",
      "why": "It establishes that ports are not just transport hubs but pivotal institutional and physical nodes capable of coordinating energy infrastructure and accelerating niche-technology diffusion across previously siloed systems."
    }
